  "problem": "The joint CDF of two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1\\text{ or }y<1 \\\\ \\frac{4({x}^{2}-1)(y-1)}{9y}, & 1\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 4 \\\\ {F}_{X}(x), & 1\\le x\\le 2,\\,y>4 \\\\ {F}_{Y}(y), & x>2,\\,1\\le y\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>2,\\,y>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${F}_{X}$ and ${F}_{Y}$ are the marginal CDFs of $X$ and $Y,$ respectively. Find the joint PDF $f(x,y)$ for $1\\le x\\le 2$ and $1\\le y\\le 4.$",
